Qt audio smoke, bead VieNeuTTSApp-3iy, deselected); 100% line coverage on the
new module.

Design: the store is the only writer of clone metadata, so the spec's rules are
enforced where no caller can bypass them — clone_requirements come from
engine_profiles capabilities (Base: reference clip + transcript + consent;
VieNeu: no transcript; CustomVoice: refuses), the reference clip is validated
(WAV-only, readable, 1-30 s) and re-written as an app-owned mono float32 copy at
its own sample rate, and dedup is keyed on (profile, sha256 of the source bytes,
transcript) so a double submit returns the existing clone with one file on disk.
Atomicity: reference copy first (temp + os.replace, 4 attempts for Windows
sharing violations), index second; an index failure deletes the copy it was
about to publish, and a removal writes the index before unlinking the audio so a
failed unlink leaves a harmless orphan instead of a dangling entry. Corruption
handling is deliberately non-destructive: an unparseable index is quarantined as
clones.json.corrupt (metadata recoverable), per-entry validation drops bad
entries with a warning, and index paths are always re-resolved inside the store
root so a hand-edited absolute/escaping path cannot point the model host at an
arbitrary file. prompt_for() is the resolver Task 4.2 will pass as
QwenEngineProvider(clone_prompt_for=...).
